meta {
  name: qnib-ftest
  seq: 5
}

auth {
  mode: inherit
}

vars:pre-request {
  repo: qnib/ftest
  tag: latest
}

docs {
  Inspect the qnib/ftest artefacts populated by `metahub-admin parse
  collections` (pullthrough-repo session).

  Run order (all requests inherit Bearer auth from the `auth` folder
  — run `auth/get` then `auth/getToken` once per session to set
  `oci_bearer` in the active environment):

    1. getTagsList         — confirm the Tag is discoverable
    2. headIndexByTag      — the Slot's computed :Index, content-negotiated
                             as an OCI image-index (regression guard #10)
    3. getIndexByTag       — same, but the body; post-script extracts
                             `indexDigest` + `childManifestDigest` into
                             env vars used by the next requests
    4. getIndexByDigest    — round-trip the Index by its own digest
    5. headChildManifest   — HEAD the first per-arch manifest referenced
                             from the Index
    6. getChildManifest    — GET same; post-script extracts `configDigest`
                             and `firstLayerDigest`
    7. getConfigBlob       — GET the image config blob (from `blobs`
                             bucket; was key=metahub-api-dev after the
                             pipeline-repo bucket-alignment fix)
    8. headLayerBlob       — HEAD the first layer blob
    9. neo4jSlotChain      — out-of-band: hit Neo4j's HTTP tx endpoint
                             to confirm `(Slot)-[:POINTS_TO]->(Index)`
                             count — matches pipeline Verify-CE #9

  The complete chain is what `manifest-tool inspect <registry>/qnib/ftest:latest`
  performs under the hood. Having each step as a separate Bruno
  request makes intermediate debugging (which step 404s, which digest
  doesn't resolve) straightforward.
}
